  {
    "case_id": "assembly.bad.primer_pair_tm_delta",
    "capability": "assembly",
    "expect_overall": "warn",
    "expect_check": "primer.pair_tm_delta",
    "expect_severity": "warn",
    "rationale": "The two primers of the pair are pinned to real slices whose melting temperatures differ by more than the 5.0 C threshold, while each one stays inside the 10 C band that would make primer.tm_in_range fail. That separation is the whole point: a pair can be individually acceptable and still be unusable together, because one thermocycling program has to serve both and the annealing temperature that suits the hotter primer leaves the cooler one unbound. primer.pair_tm_delta is the only check that compares the two primers of a pair, so it is the only one that can catch this. Every sequence in this case is a plus strand slice of a real GenBank record already in this repository, at the offset the fragment source field records. The offsets are chosen, the bases are not.",
