    "rationale": "The forward primer is a real 22 bp slice that folds back on itself with a stem that includes its own 3' terminus. A 3' stem is the damaging case, because it sequesters the base the polymerase has to extend from, so the primer does not prime at all rather than merely competing with annealing. That is why section 7.5 check 6 is FAIL for a 3' stem past the hard threshold and WARN for an internal one, and primer.hairpin is the only check that folds a primer against itself. hairpin_engine is pinned to window in every assembly gold case. ViennaRNA is an optional import that is not in requirements.txt, so leaving the engine on auto would make the verdict depend on whether the package happens to be installed, which section 3.3 constraint 1 forbids for a gold set.",
