    "expect_severity": "warn",
    "rationale": "The fragment is 11,135 bp, over the 10,000 bp ceiling that the standard high fidelity polymerase protocol is documented to. An amplicon this long needs a long range polymerase, a longer extension time and a different protocol, and attempting it with the default program gives either no product or a smear. assembly.amplicon_size is the only check that measures the expected product length, so it is the one that must catch it, and it is a WARN because a long amplicon is achievable with the right enzyme rather than impossible. The fragment is a concatenation of whole real records already in this repository, assembled only to reach a length past the ceiling without inventing a single base; the EF1A record appears twice, in the interior only, so that both primer binding regions stay unique and primer.specificity_in_template is not the check that fires.",
